 :admission-model {:separate-facts
                   {:owner-admission "The controlled fake owner may admit an exact event at an exact predecessor head, event ID, resulting head and revision before a response is delivered. In P1 this is inert synthetic schedule data, not a call to or proof about a real owner."
                    :ack-delivery "A later response is merely delivery of a result. A matching trusted synthetic proof must bind exact event bytes/identity, predecessor, resulting head, revision and accepted status; generation/lease staleness affects publication, not whether the event was admitted. Wrong, conflicting, unauthenticated or incomplete evidence cannot establish admission."
                    :local-lease "Freshness is a separate local lease bound to generation, candidate cut, head and deadline. Loss, gap, timeout, changed generation or expiry revokes it immediately. A late accepted ACK or trusted head resolution accounts for history but never revives the old lease."}
                   :head-discipline "Maintain a bounded pending event identity and exact expected predecessor; once admission is possible, never issue a different baseline, reconciliation or competing event until the outcome and authoritative exact head are resolved. A verified matching accepted result advances the known head and revision even if its response is stale; an explicit rejection tied to the same identity and unchanged trusted head permits a new attempt only under normal bounded rules. An unknown outcome, untrusted proof, mismatch or head ambiguity remains uncertain and requires later trusted owner-head resolution. No blind retry as a new event, fabricated acceptance or conflicting initial baseline. Checked deadlines/generation and no-freshness rules still apply."
                   :stale-baseline-or-reconciliation "When matching proof establishes that a baseline or reconciliation was admitted before a subsequent loss, first account for its exact head, event ID and revision. Keep the lease revoked; submit one catalog-valid coverage-gap at that admitted revision and causal predecessor/head. Only after the gap itself is proven admitted may a fresh supported-cut reconciliation directly cause that gap, use a higher revision and fresh incarnations. Do not treat the admitted baseline as absent, nor issue a second initial baseline."
                   :stale-gap "If matching proof establishes the proposed gap was admitted, account for its exact resulting head and make that event the single active gap, regardless of stale delivery; do not emit a duplicate. Keep the lease revoked and preserve uncertainty until a justified new cut and accepted, directly causal reconciliation. If its status/head is unknown, hold the pending identity and resolve the head first; no fabricated gap or competing retry."
                   :prebaseline "A loss known to precede any admitted baseline remains local uncertainty and produces no gap. If baseline admission is unresolved at loss, do not assume this case: await trustworthy exact-head resolution and branch according to the actual admitted outcome."
                   :resolution-bound "All pending records, proof fields and scheduled messages obey V2 fixed limits and constant-code failures. Resolution is a separate bounded fixture input, not an unbounded poll or live callback. If the deadline or budget expires, preserve uncertain pending identity and require a later separately initiated trusted resolution; never infer rejection from timeout."}
 :transition-overrides [{:condition :baseline-or-reconciliation-accepted-before-loss-ack-delivered-after-loss
                         :action "Verify exact acceptance evidence, advance admitted event/head/revision, keep lease revoked, and propose one lawful old-revision gap; await its proven acceptance before a new reconciliation."}
                        {:condition :admission-unknown-after-loss-or-ack-timeout
                         :action "Retain pending identity and expected predecessor; remain uncertain and request only a bounded inert head-resolution intent. Do not emit any competing baseline, reconciliation or new event. A trusted matching resolution accounts for the accepted event; rejection with verified unchanged head permits a fresh bounded attempt."}
                        {:condition :gap-accepted-before-loss-ack-delivered-late
                         :action "Verify exact accepted gap and head, mark that gap active exactly once and keep lease revoked; subsequent reconciliation must directly cause that exact gap. If evidence does not prove it, hold pending and resolve exact head first."}
                        {:condition :stale-or-wrong-ack-without-proven-admission
                         :action "No new currentness and no assertion of rejection; ambiguity remains until trusted head proof. Old generation may report history only when exact owner evidence verifies it, never operate the current lease."}]
 :deterministic-red-schedules
 {:notation "Fixture symbols below denote exact synthetic values, not real owner records: H0, H1, H2 and H3 are four distinct fixed 64-character lowercase hexadecimal fixture head tokens, respectively 64 repetitions of 0, 1, 2 and 3. They model opaque head identities; no claim they are computed ledger hashes. Every result additionally binds the exact frozen-catalog envelope and predecessor; tests use valid frozen events and actual frozen replay, with head-token consistency separately checked in the fake harness. IDs below are literal canonical UUIDs."
  :ids {:baseline "10000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001"
        :gap "10000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002"
        :reconciliation "10000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003"
        :epoch "20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001"
        :old-incarnation "30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001"
        :new-incarnation "30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002"
        :workspace "40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001"}
  :cases
  [{:id :accepted-before-loss-ack-after-loss
    :schedule ["Generation 1: supported synthetic cut proposes baseline B at revision 1, predecessor H0, epoch and old-incarnation above. Fake owner records exact B accepted H0->H1; ACK is withheld."
               "Loss revokes lease and advances generation before ACK. Deliver trusted exact B/H0/H1/revision-1 acceptance from old generation. Account H1 and B without granting lease. Emit exactly one gap G at revision 1 with predecessor H1 and correct causal predecessor B."
               "Fake owner accepts G H1->H2; only after proven acceptance propose reconciliation R at revision 2, predecessor H2, direct cause G and fresh new-incarnation; fake acceptance is H2->H3."]
    :assert "Frozen replay of [B G R] accepts, reports fresh-at-cut only as offline projection, retains historical gap and old window-history, retires old lifetime and uses new incarnation. Fixture lease is absent until a separately supported unexpired new cut and matching R admission; the stale B ACK never restores it. No second initial baseline or duplicate gap."}
   {:id :lost-ack-then-resolved-head
    :schedule ["Fake owner accepts B revision 1 H0->H1 but its ACK is permanently lost; loss/timeout occurs while outcome remains unknown."
               "While unresolved, deliver no fabricated failure: assert pending B/H0 and no competing baseline, gap or reconciliation. Feed a bounded trusted synthetic head-resolution result binding exact B bytes, ID, H0, H1 and revision 1."
               "Account H1 with revoked lease; propose G at revision 1 after B. Prove G H1->H2, then R H2->H3 directly causes G and advances revision 2 with fresh incarnation."]
    :assert "Frozen replay [B G R] retains gap, never treats B as absent, and never attributes live freshness to resolution. Wrong-ID, wrong predecessor, wrong resulting head, missing event bytes, untrusted proof and unresolved timeout leave the pending identity uncertain and produce no conflicting event. A separately verified rejection plus unchanged H0 is the only branch allowing a new initial attempt."}
   {:id :stale-gap-ack
    :schedule ["Begin with proven admitted B/H1 at revision 1 and fixture lease; loss revokes lease and proposes G at old revision 1, predecessor H1, direct cause B."
               "Fake owner accepts G H1->H2, but ACK is delayed past a further generation change. Deliver trusted exact G/H1/H2/revision-1 acceptance from old generation. Account H2 and make G the one active gap without a second admission intent."
               "At a later supported synthetic cut propose R at revision 2 directly causing G, with fresh new-incarnation; fake owner accepts H2->H3."]
    :assert "Frozen replay [B G] is uncertain with active G, [B G R] has historical gap and fresh-at-cut projection; old lease remains revoked and stale gap ACK never makes current. Missing or conflicting gap proof leaves pending G and blocks duplicate or reconciliation. Replayed memberships contain only current windows; historical membership evidence is in immutable B and window-history."}
   {:id :stale-reconciliation-ack
    :schedule ["Given proven B/H1 then G/H2, fake owner accepts R revision 2 H2->H3 with direct cause G; lose coverage before R ACK arrives. A trusted exact late ACK accounts R/H3, without a lease."
               "Emit one new distinct coverage-gap at old revision 2, causally following R and predecessor H3; do not reuse G. Await its verified admission before any further reconciliation."]
    :assert "Frozen replay of B/G/R followed by the new admitted gap is uncertain, retains both historical gap facts and prevents targeting; no old acknowledgement revives a lease."}]}
